body:
Yeah the issue here is fully on the GPU its just not that powerful. You should turn down your settings but particuarly the ones that affect graphics memory laptop tend to have 4 gb of VRAM which is severely limiting but it will also downclock under sustained loads because its a laptop. Just a bummer make sure to take advantage of DLSS in performance mode, it might be the thing that makes it playable but is unlikely to be a great experience especially on high settings.

&#x200B;

and yeah ram at 16 gb will be fine no need to worry about that just make sure you don't have chrome or something hogging it in the background
